  ! roster for 2026 is PROJECTED, not published — the off-ballot drop below is
    running against an ASSUMPTION about who will contest, not against a result
    file.
      parties  82
      file     data/processed/pools_2026.json  (field `roster`)
      source   roster_source='declared'; reach='2021 ward ballot, carried
               forward unchanged; 80 declared in judgements'
      how      a nomination list typed by hand into
               judgements/joburg-2026.toml under `[roster]`. If that table
               says `complete = true` it REPLACES the projection and licenses
               deleting the parties it omits; if it does not, it is UNIONED
               with the projection (the preceding LGE result and national
               baseline, less the JUDGEMENT-CALLS.md §K1/§K2 floors) and
               removes nobody. Read the emit's own `[roster]` line to see
               which happened.
      ends     you have ALREADY declared a list, and this warning still fires,
               because `published` means 2026's own RESULT file —
               `roster_for_target` branches on
               `cityconfig.CALENDAR['2026'].results`, which stays None until
               the election has been held and ingested. So the state clears
               AFTER polling day, never before it. What you can still do
               before then: confirm the list is the WHOLE ballot and set
               `complete = true` in judgements/joburg-2026.toml, which is what
               licenses deleting the parties it omits, then re-emit.
      scored   NOT SCORED. When the real ballot lands nothing compares it with
               the roster above, so this projection is never marked right or
               wrong and the next one is no better informed. See MACHINERY.md,
               "Scoring the projected roster".
